  "must_fix": [
    "training_workloads/unified_h1/robustness.py:164–173 selects the first low-speed window before checking its preceding signed-motion prerequisite, then never searches for a later eligible confirmation. Read-only CPU counterexample: W-near lane0, initial sensor=(4.7,0,2), zero initial velocity; post-step normal velocities are 0 for indices0–11, .05 at12, .1 at13–23, .05 at24, then0. Integrating with linear ramps gives minimum clearance1.18m, no trigger/height/collision/reset violation, 11 qualifying motion observations followed by valid stop confirmation at index34 (3.5s), and296 hold observations. Written proactive20s/101-observation rules are satisfied, but scorer chooses index10 and returns movement_prerequisite=false. Select the first confirmation whose entire low-speed window follows completed signed motion, while retaining the original start/clearance-trigger deadline and all hold/safety gates. Add this early-startup-rest positive regression alongside the existing late-motion negative test; do not restart or extend the deadline."
